{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.45,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["T3", "T7"],
      "pins": ["T3.1", "T3.2", "T3.3", "T7.1", "T7.2", "T7.3", "H1.2"],
      "nets": ["/NET0076", "/NET0067", "/+24V_{F}", "+24V", "/NET0015"],
      "observed": "The ATO valve low-side switch T3 is an AO3400A (N-channel, SOT-23-3, 5.7 A) in the netlist. Its drain drives the ATO valve connector H1 pin 2 (/NET0067). The AON6407 (8-DFN) sits in T7, a P-channel device between /+24V_F and +24V with its gate on /NET0015.",
      "expected": "The specification says the ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch is an AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) driven through R10 (100 Ω) from T4 (BT3904). The AO3400A is not part of that role, and the AON6407 should be the ATO switch.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"T3\") (value \"AO3400A\") (footprint \"Coert-Vonk:MOSFET N-CH 30V 5.7A AO3400A SOT23-3L\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"T7\") (value \"AON6407\") (footprint \"Coert-Vonk:MOSFET P-CH 30V 32A 10mΩ AON6407\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"T3\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"D\") (pintype \"power_out\"))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "T3 — AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) | ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch"}
      ],
      "impact": "The ATO valve is switched by a small-signal SOT-23 MOSFET rather than the intended 8-DFN power part, while the higher-current AON6407 is used in the reverse-polarity position. This changes the thermal and current margin of the ATO switch and the BOM build may not match the design.",
      "confidence": 0.45
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U4"],
      "pins": ["U4.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(U4-EN-Pad2)"],
      "observed": "The EN pin (pin 2) of the TPS62933 buck regulator U4 is not connected to any net.",
      "expected": "The EN pin of a TPS62933 should be tied to a defined level, such as VIN through a divider or a logic signal, rather than left floating.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"149\") (name \"unconnected-(U4-EN-Pad2)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"EN\") (pintype \"input+no_connect\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the part does not have a guaranteed internal pull on EN, the 24 V to 5 V converter may start or stop unpredictably, which would affect the +5V and +3V3 rails.",
      "confidence": 0.2
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The most likely deviation is that the ATO valve switch T3 is an AO3400A, while the specification places the AON6407 in that role and the AON6407 appears in a different reverse-polarity position. The second item, a floating EN pin on the buck regulator, is a lower-confidence concern."
}

